Patch for src/main/java/com/aria/integration/service/IntegrationOutboundCaller.java (Module 6).

Why: every outbound call is written to integration_event_log with redact(payload). redact() only
masks keys containing password / secret / token / apikey / authorization, so the installation-report
one-time code would be stored in plain text: in the SMS "variables" and inside the email "body".
After this patch a payload with "sensitive": true has its body / variables masked, and any key
containing "otp" is masked as well.

--- a/src/main/java/com/aria/integration/service/IntegrationOutboundCaller.java
+++ b/src/main/java/com/aria/integration/service/IntegrationOutboundCaller.java
@@ private static Map<String, Object> redact(Map<String, Object> in) {
         if (in == null) return null;
+        boolean sensitive = Boolean.TRUE.equals(in.get("sensitive"));
         Map<String, Object> out = new HashMap<>();
         for (var e : in.entrySet()) {
             String k = e.getKey();
             if (k == null) continue;
             String lk = k.toLowerCase();
             if (lk.contains("password") || lk.contains("secret")
                     || lk.contains("token") || lk.contains("apikey")
-                    || lk.contains("authorization")) {
+                    || lk.contains("authorization") || lk.contains("otp")
+                    || (sensitive && (lk.equals("body") || lk.equals("variables")))) {
                 out.put(k, "***");
             } else if (e.getValue() instanceof Map<?,?> m) {
